# Codebase labels

Full map: [docs/codebase-map.md](../../docs/codebase-map.md)

| Label | Paths |
|-------|--------|
| **surface** | `src/app/**` |
| **ui** | `src/components/**` |
| **read-model** | `src/lib/queries/**` |
| **engine** | `src/lib/engine/**` |
| **clinical** | `src/lib/clinical/**`, `src/lib/pa/**` |
| **nps** | `src/lib/nps/**` |
| **integrity** | `src/lib/integrity/**`, `src/lib/agents/**` |
| **platform** | `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/lib/pg-sql.ts`, `src/lib/auth.ts`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/lib/jobs.ts` |
| **schema** | `prisma/**` |
| **ops** | `scripts/**`, `fly.toml`, `docs/**` |
| **proof** | `tests/**` |

Rules of thumb:

- Pages call **read-model** loaders; keep heavy SQL out of page files.
- **engine** changes need **proof** tests.
- Raw SQL must be Postgres-safe (`GROUP BY`, dates as `Date` not epoch ms). See `src/lib/pg-sql.ts`.
- Long book scans (NPS/experience) stay sequential — do not `Promise.all` pool-heavy queries behind PgBouncer.
